{
  "slug": "verbos-regulares",
  "number": 5,
  "part": 2,
  "title": "Regular verbs in the present",
  "tagline": "The -er, -ir and -re groups, and why four forms sound the same.",
  "goal": "Conjugate any regular -er, -ir (like finir) and -re (like vendre) verb in the present and know which forms sound the same.",
  "minutes": 10,
  "sections": [
    {
      "id": "receta",
      "title": "Stem + ending",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "English verbs barely change (I speak, he speak**s**). French verbs have a different ending for almost every person, but regular verbs follow a simple recipe:"
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "Take the infinitive: *parler* (to speak).",
            "Remove the ending (-er, -ir, -re) to get the **stem**: *parl-*.",
            "Add the ending for each person: *je parl{e}*."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "This works for thousands of verbs. You can look up any verb in the **Verbs** section."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "tone": "note",
          "text": "The French present covers both «I speak» and «I'm speaking»: *je parle* means either. There's no separate -ing form."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "er",
      "title": "-er verbs",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "About 90 % of French verbs belong here."
        },
        {
          "type": "conjugation",
          "persons": [
            "je",
            "tu",
            "il / elle / on",
            "nous",
            "vous",
            "ils / elles"
          ],
          "verbs": [
            {
              "verb": "parler",
              "meaning": "to speak",
              "forms": [
                "je parl{e}",
                "tu parl{es}",
                "il parl{e}",
                "nous parl{ons}",
                "vous parl{ez}",
                "ils parl{ent}"
              ],
              "notes": [
                "**-e**",
                "**-es**",
                "**-e**",
                "**-ons**",
                "**-ez**",
                "**-ent**"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**To start with:** *aimer* (to love, to like), *manger* (to eat), *regarder* (to watch), *écouter* (to listen), *habiter* (to live), *travailler* (to work), *jouer* (to play), *étudier* (to study)."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "tone": "warning",
          "text": "*aller* (to go) ends in -er but is irregular: *je vais, tu vas…* See [[9]]."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "sonido",
      "title": "Four forms, one sound",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "In -er verbs, **je, tu, il and ils sound exactly the same**:"
        },
        {
          "type": "formula",
          "text": "je parle = tu parles = il parle = ils parlent",
          "caption": "All are pronounced «parl»."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The endings *-e*, *-es* and *-ent* are **silent**. Only *nous parlons* («par-lohn») and *vous parlez* («par-lay») sound different."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "tone": "warning",
          "text": "A classic mistake: pronouncing the *-ent* of *ils parlent*. It is never pronounced."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "tone": "tip",
          "text": "When writing, the sound won't help you: the subject decides the ending."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ir",
      "title": "-ir verbs like finir",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "You can spot them by the **-iss-** in the plural."
        },
        {
          "type": "conjugation",
          "persons": [
            "je",
            "tu",
            "il / elle / on",
            "nous",
            "vous",
            "ils / elles"
          ],
          "verbs": [
            {
              "verb": "finir",
              "meaning": "to finish",
              "forms": [
                "je fin{is}",
                "tu fin{is}",
                "il fin{it}",
                "nous fin{issons}",
                "vous fin{issez}",
                "ils fin{issent}"
              ],
              "notes": [
                "**-is**",
                "**-is**",
                "**-it**",
                "**-issons**",
                "**-issez**",
                "**-issent**"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**Same group:** *choisir* (to choose), *réussir* (to succeed, to pass), *grandir* (to grow up), *remplir* (to fill), *réfléchir* (to think, to reflect), *obéir* (to obey)."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "tone": "warning",
          "text": "Not every -ir verb follows this model: *partir, dormir, sortir* are irregular (*je pars, nous partons*). The *-iss-* is the giveaway."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "re",
      "title": "-re verbs like vendre",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "conjugation",
          "persons": [
            "je",
            "tu",
            "il / elle / on",
            "nous",
            "vous",
            "ils / elles"
          ],
          "verbs": [
            {
              "verb": "vendre",
              "meaning": "to sell",
              "forms": [
                "je vend{s}",
                "tu vend{s}",
                "il vend",
                "nous vend{ons}",
                "vous vend{ez}",
                "ils vend{ent}"
              ],
              "notes": [
                "**-s**",
                "**-s**",
                "— (nothing)",
                "**-ons**",
                "**-ez**",
                "**-ent**"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**Same group:** *attendre* (to wait), *répondre* (to answer), *entendre* (to hear), *perdre* (to lose), *descendre* (to go down)."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "tone": "note",
          "text": "In the singular the d is silent (*je vends* = «vahn», nasal); in the plural you hear it: *ils vendent* = «vahnd»."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ortografia",
      "title": "Spelling adjustments",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Some -er verbs change with *nous* to keep their soft sound:"
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "**-ger → nous -geons**: *manger → nous mang{e}ons*, *voyager → nous voyag{e}ons*.",
            "**-cer → nous -çons**: *commencer → nous commen{ç}ons*."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "And elision: *je* + *aime* = *j'aime*; *je* + *écoute* = *j'écoute*."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "exercises": [
